(:id "port/moo/vt/widening" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/mootable/widening_test.go: TestMooWireSignalingNaNWideningAndLEBOverflow, TestMooWideningLadder, TestMooMapReadReports" "internal/codegen/mootable/widening_test.go: TestMooWideningNegativeControl (float-rung, leb-tenth, map-key-once, kind-mismatch)" "internal/codegen/mootable/refusalreasons_test.go: TestMooLoadRefusalReasons, TestMooLoadRefusalReasonsNegativeControl/refusing-counters") :tested-revision "aa64dfdfcdaef01e567f9bc2403995167cd30e2b" :note "2026-11-08 STRICT-100: re-pinned as a strict verdict against the Go reference engine (internal/tablewire Decode, Encode). The 12x10 ladder answers the reference's verdict on every cell (21 widenings load with the reference's widened and save its bytes; 89 narrowing or cross-kind cells refuse the whole read); a float32 under a float64 widens exactly, and a NaN or an infinity refuses; a LEB tenth byte past 2^64 is refused; a map's widened key counts once per map, and a descending, repeated or other-kind key refuses whole. No reason name and no repair counter is compared (docs/rulings.json refusal-verdict-only). The four controls (the float rung, the LEB tenth-byte clause, once-per-map widening, the load's kind_mismatch refusal) each turn their gates red. Also green on a local merge with #2963 (phase one). Run on vision (Linux x86-64) under the pinned moo f60f0239, SCHEMA_SLOW=1 SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1.")
(:id "port/moo/vt/wire-fuzzer" :state :todo :tested-revision "08af4a4cace63fc734f86225e7ec85509279f7d9" :note "2026-11-03: Open: the cell's acceptance is a passing nightly-readiness receipt, and test/conformance/nightly-readiness moo at main 08af4a4ca ends INCOMPLETE on one phase, external-table-gates. Its make tables-moo-compiler-claims runs compiler/tablesmoo_test.go, where TestMooRegistersItsTableCarriers and TestMooRefusesTheConstructsItDoesNotCarryByName still require MOO to refuse required, forms, unbounded text and array root, which MOO carries (PR #2750). Every fuzz phase of that run passes: wire-plain-1..3 (275 seeds over 64 roots, 262099 mutants each, 0 divergences), wire-retain-1..3 (110 seeds over 28 roots, 191410 mutants each, 0 divergences) and the wire-fuzz negative control. make tables-moo-release exits 0 at 08af4a4ca: plain seeds 1-3 at 262099 mutants and retain seeds 1-3 at 191410 mutants pass, with the negative control and the usage example and its control. Run on vision (Linux x86-64), clean clone, siblings at the ci-full.yml pins.")
(:id "port/moo/vt/retain-unknown" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/mootable/retain_test.go: TestMooRetainAnswersTheManifest, TestMooRetainMatchesTheGoEngine, TestMooRetainMeasureAndIdempotence, TestMooRetainRefusesWhatThePageRefuses, TestMooRetainRefusesANonFiniteRetainedFloat" "internal/codegen/mootable/retain_occurrence_test.go: TestMooRetainOccurrencesMatchTheGoEngine, TestMooRetainDamagedParentDiscardsTheWholeLoad" "internal/codegen/mootable/retain_test.go: TestMooRetainNegativeControl, TestMooRetainDifferentialNegativeControl (save-tail/manifest, save-tail/evolved, save-tail/occurrence, keeps-damage/occurrence)" "./build/conformance-harness run --only moo: retain pass 8/8, retain-save pass 7/7") :tested-revision "411019d677b5a539db74de9413b8bd5cf8faeb56" :note "2026-11-08 STRICT-100: re-pinned as a strict verdict against the Go reference engine (internal/tablewire DecodeRetain, EncodeRetain). Every `retain` manifest row (the strict cut's 8-field row) loads whole and saves its pinned file byte for byte; the manifest rows, the evolved pairs and the 25 occurrence wires give the Go engine's verdict (damage and a repeated field refuse whole, a refusal defines nothing else, no reason compared), and where both answer the value the store bytes, the evolution diagnostics and the saved bytes agree. The controls plant out the save's write of a kept record, and the damage discards with phase one; each differential goes red. TestMooRetainConstructsMatchTheGoEngine no longer exists and is not cited. Run on the studio under the pinned moo f60f0239, SCHEMA_SLOW=1, with #2963 (phase one) under it.")
